+  // nlearn: SPIR-V cooperative-matrix component-wise arithmetic (spirv.FMul etc.)
+  // is only defined for f16/f32/f64 fragments; a bf16 coop matrix supports ONLY
+  // MulAdd (matmul), not elementwise. A bf16 PROLOGUE elementwise (e.g. the SwiGLU
+  // gate feeding w2, or a fused A*A on a matmul input) writes the promoted A/B tile
+  // and, having a transfer_write user (not the contract directly), infers COp and
+  // gets absorbed into an illegal `spirv.FMul` on coopmatrix<...xbf16, MatrixAcc>
